<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Adaptive icon background (Android 8+).

  The launcher masks this 108x108dp layer down to whatever shape the OEM uses
  (circle, squircle, rounded square, teardrop), so only the centre 72dp is
  guaranteed visible and only the centre 66dp is guaranteed safe. A background
  therefore must be a full-bleed fill, never a shape with corners — the corners
  get cropped and the icon looks off-centre on a circular launcher.

  Flat `AppColors.darkSurface` (#141417), deliberately.

  The mark is a gradient ring running deep indigo (bottom-left) through magenta
  to amber (top-right). Two other treatments were rendered and rejected:

    * the brand gradient as the background — the ring's own gradient runs along
      the same axis, so the left half of the ring vanished into it;
    * white — legible, but a white plate on the home screen is the exact
      "this app is not finished" defect this adaptive icon was added to remove.

  A flat dark tile keeps the whole ring readable at every density and matches
  the dark-first UI the icon opens into.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <path
        android:pathData="M0,0 h108 v108 h-108 z"
        android:fillColor="#FF141417" />
</vector>
